  "properties": {
    "title": "Research Vessel Conductivity Temperature Depth (CTD) Profiles",	
    "description": "Conductivity–Temperature–Depth (CTD) profiles collected from research vessels. Most, but not all, of the CTD data is from vessels that are participating in the GO‑SHIP repeat hydrography programme. These high‑quality, full‑depth ocean profiles provide essential measurements of temperature, salinity, pressure, and, where available, dissolved oxygen using research‑grade instrumentation. All observations follow internationally agreed GO‑SHIP best practices, undergo rigorous quality control, and are provided in standardised formats to ensure global interoperability. These data form part of the Global Ocean Observing System (GOOS) and support long‑term climate monitoring, detection of water‑mass changes, validation of ocean models, and scientific research requiring authoritative subsurface ocean measurements.",	
